      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>A rahit (a chain piyyut before the silluq) for the second day of Rosh haShanah, by R. Shimon bar Isaac “the Great” of Mainz. Here translated preserving the acrostic, slightly edited from its form as part of a day 2 service maḥzor I designed two years ago.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>Note: “<j:divineName>The CAUSE</j:divineName>” is used to translate the Divine Name <j:divineName>YHVH</j:divineName>, based on the philosophical idea of <j:divineName>God</j:divineName> as the <j:divineName>Prime Mover</j:divineName> and on the interpretation of <j:divineName>the Name</j:divineName> as a causative form of the copula – “causes to be.” All divine referents (pronouns, epithets, names) are rendered in unicase.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_57936_introduction"/>
